            0.215,
            0.068,
            0.816,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Predicting What Comes Next: Exploring Sequences and Progressions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.844,
            0.068,
            0.884,
            0.085
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "185"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.108,
            0.886,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first known written mention of this result can be found in Āryabhaṭa’s Āryabhaṭīya, Chapter 2, Verse 19. The verse provides two ways to calculate the sum, with the second part describing that the sum can be calculated by taking the sum of the first and last terms, divided by two (the average), and multiplied by the number of terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.225,
            0.399,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.262,
            0.598,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you use this formula to find "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{S}_{20}, \\mathrm{S}_{50}   or   \\mathrm{S}_{1000}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.303,
            0.884,
            0.343
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Also, this formula can be used to find the sum of consecutive numbers such as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "25+26+27+\\cdots+58"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.349,
            0.884,
            0.37
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "Note that   25 + 26 + 27 + \\cdots + 58 = (1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 58) - (1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 24)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.374,
            0.821,
            0.415
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{S}_{58}-\\mathrm{S}_{24}=\\frac{58 \\times 59}{2}-\\frac{24 \\times 25}{2}=29 \\times 59-12 \\times 25=1711-300=1411."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.438,
            0.399,
            0.461
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.475,
            0.855,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us revisit the sequence "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { \\mathrm { n } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of triangular numbers 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, … shown in Fig. 8.1. Note that the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term of this sequence is the sum of the first n natural numbers. Thus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t_{n}=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.554,
            0.779,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you use this to find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } } , 1 7 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "8 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " triangular numbers?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.374,
            0.625,
            0.621,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 8.2"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.673,
            0.731,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 6 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " terms of the AP: 3, 8, 13, 18, …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.701,
            0.884,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Which term of the AP : 21, 18, 15, … is – 81? Also, is 0 a term of this AP? Give reasons for your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.749,
            0.884,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term of the AP: 11, 8, 5, 2 … Write the recursive rule for this AP."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.796,
            0.884,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. An AP consists of 50 terms in which the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 ^ { \\mathrm { r d } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term is 12 and the last term is 106. Find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 9 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.834,
            0.886,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the first term and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\text{\" } \\mathrm{d} \\text{\" }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the common difference, then we arrive at the equations "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a + 2d = 12"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a + 49d = 106"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Solve this pair of linear equations for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } d ^ { \\flat } . )"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
